✅ Pre-Install Sanity Check
Config & Dotfiles
MangoWM config + your END-4 quickshell fork backed up (GitHub or WettamSnapsMain)
.config/ folder included in the home backup — double-check quickshell, MangoWM, and any bar configs are in there
OBS scenes/profiles if you had those set up


Package Lists
Official packages: pacman -Qqen > pkg-official.list
AUR packages: pacman -Qqem > pkg-aur.list
Both saved to WettamSnapsMain so they survive the wipe


🔐 Most Common — Make the Folder + Scripts Executable

bash
chmod 755 ~/scripts

This gives you (owner) full read/write/execute, and everyone else read/execute. Good default for a scripts folder.

To also make everything inside executable recursively:
bash
chmod -R 755 ~/scripts


⚡ Just Make Scripts Executable (Without Touching Permissions on the Folder)
bash
chmod +x ~/scripts/*.sh

Or recursively for all .sh files nested inside:
bash
find ~/scripts -name "*.sh" -exec chmod +x {} \;


🔒 If It's Personal Scripts Only (Tighter Security)
bash
chmod 700 ~/scripts





